---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import questions from '../data/questions.json';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';

const byCategory = [...new Set(questions.map((q) => q.category))]
  .map((c) => ({ c, n: questions.filter((q) => q.category === c).length }))
  .sort((a, b) => a.c.localeCompare(b.c));
---

<Base title="About" description="What this site is, where the content comes from, and how to use it.">
  <h1>About this site</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A free, no-login study aid for the Hanford Radiological Control Technician
    (RCT) recertification exam.
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Browse the <a href={withBase('/chapters')}>chapters and learning objectives</a> to see what each module covers.</li>
    <li>Pick a test: a full exam for a book, one chapter, or a single objective. Questions are drawn at random.</li>
    <li>Answer at your own pace. Press <strong>Check answer</strong> to see right away whether you were correct.</li>
    <li>Press <strong>Submit</strong> any time. If you stop early, only the questions you answered are scored.</li>
    <li>Review every answer, then retake the questions you missed or take a fresh draw.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What it is</h2>
  <p>
    Two things: downloadable study guides (PDFs) and browser-based practice
    tests that score you and explain every answer. It is a static website &mdash;
    there is no server, no account, and no tracking. Your results are saved only in this
    browser on this device (see <a href={withBase('/progress')}>My progress</a>) and are never sent anywhere.
  </p>

  <h2>What it is not</h2>
  <p>
    This site is <strong>unofficial</strong>. It is not affiliated with, endorsed
    by, or maintained by the U.S. Department of Energy, Hanford Mission
    Integration Solutions, or any other site contractor. The practice questions
    are written for study and may not match the wording, weighting, or scope of
    the real exam. Always defer to your current site procedures and official
    reference material (10 CFR 835, DOE-STD-1098, DOE-HDBK-1122, and your
    facility's RWPs and RPPs).
  </p>

  <h2>Question bank</h2>
  <p>Current coverage:</p>
  <table class="downloads">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Topic area</th><th>Questions</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {byCategory.map((row) => (
        <tr>
          <td>{row.c}</td>
          <td>{row.n}</td>
        </tr>
      ))}
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Total</strong></td>
        <td><strong>{questions.length}</strong></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>
    Found a wrong answer or an outdated reference? The content lives in
    <code>src/data/questions.json</code>. Fixes are welcome via whatever channel
    the site owner has set up (repo issue or pull request).
  </p>
</Base>
